Keep the satellite libraries when the linker dead-strips (macOS only).

The graphics and error-reporting libraries are link-time plugins: libast
refers to their symbols without linking against them, so a program holds no
direct reference to them.  On macOS libast is linked -undefined
dynamic_lookup, which records no undefined symbols at all, so the linker
cannot see the satellite libraries are needed and the -Wl,-dead_strip_dylibs
in conda-forge's LDFLAGS drops all five.  The lookups then bind to nothing
and the first call through one segfaults -- for astPutErr, the first error
report of the run.  Ten of the C tests died that way, all of them tests that
deliberately provoke an error.

Force a reference to one symbol from each library so the linker keeps it.
The libraries are disjoint -- each supplies the part of the grf interface
added at the version it is named for -- so one symbol each is needed.

Only the C tests are touched, which is all this recipe builds
(--without-fortran).  The flags cannot go on the Fortran test link lines:
libtool leaves $wl empty for the Fortran tag and rewrites -Wl,-u,sym to a
bare "-u sym", which flang rejects.

This is the macOS half of the upstream fix, applied to the generated
ast_tester/Makefile.in so that no reconfiguration is needed.  Upstream does
it in configure.ac, keyed on host_os, reaching the tests through
AST_PLUGIN_KEEP in ast_tester/Makefile.am; nothing outside Darwin needs any
of it.  Remove this patch when the recipe moves to a release carrying that
fix.

--- ast_tester/Makefile.in.orig
+++ ast_tester/Makefile.in
@@ -1412,7 +1412,7 @@
     $(top_srcdir)/build-aux/tap-driver.sh
 
 TAP_LOG_COMPILER = $(SHELL)
-CTEST_LDADD = @LIBPAL@ @LIBCMINPACK@ \
+CTEST_LDADD = -Wl,-u,_astPutErr_ -Wl,-u,_astGAttr -Wl,-u,_astGCap -Wl,-u,_astGBBuf -Wl,-u,_astG3DAttr @LIBPAL@ @LIBCMINPACK@ \
     $(top_builddir)/libast.la \
     $(top_builddir)/libast_grf_3.2.la \
     $(top_builddir)/libast_grf_5.6.la \
